class:: EnvelopeSkewness
summary:: Asymmetry of the envelope energy distribution over time
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Amplitude

description::
The third energy-weighted central time moment divided by the temporal variance to the power 1.5. Positive values indicate a tail toward newer frames; negative values indicate a tail toward older frames. Degenerate variance returns zero.

Frames contain nonoverlapping RMS measurements. Output stays zero until a complete observation window is available, then updates once per RMS frame. Silence returns zero. Runtime cost is linear in windowTime/frameTime per update; there is no callback allocation. These descriptors are rolling summaries and do not segment individual events. Formulas are independently implemented from standard weighted moments and linear regression.

The nearest vanilla building block is link::Classes/Amplitude::, which tracks instantaneous level; this UGen summarizes its recent distribution in time.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate signal.

argument:: windowTime
Initialization-time observation duration, 2*frameTime through 10 seconds. Rounded up to whole RMS frames.

argument:: frameTime
Initialization-time RMS frame duration, 0.001 through 0.1 seconds.

argument:: floorDB
Silence floor in dBFS, clipped to -160..0. Used by dynamic complexity and dB regression; temporal moments use the original energy.

returns::
Dimensionless signed skewness.

examples::
EnvelopeSkewness calculates the third energy-weighted temporal moment divided by variance^1.5, measuring temporal asymmetry between attack and decay. A sharp percussive onset with long exponential decay produces positive skewness; backwards swells produce negative skewness. In this example, envelope skewness controls the drive of an analog wavefolder, enriching transient harmonics during sharp asymmetric plucked attacks. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: displays real-time envelope skewness.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("plucks.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic pluck fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(1.5);
            var env = EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.4), trig);
            Pluck.ar(WhiteNoise.ar * env, trig, 0.2, 1/220, 2.0, 0.3)
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var skew = EnvelopeSkewness.kr(source, windowTime: 0.5, frameTime: 0.005);
        var skewLag = skew.lag(0.08);
        var foldDrive = skewLag.linlin(0, 3, 1.0, 4.0).clip(1.0, 5.0);
        var folded = (source * foldDrive).fold2(0.5) * 0.3;
        var sound = (source * 0.2) + folded;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, skewLag.clip(-2, 4)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Envelope Skewness", ~miraBus, -2.0, 4.0, "skew");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
